  "operative_text": "Section 1 (new section of KRS Chapter 237): (2) The Department of Kentucky State Police shall issue provisional licenses to carry concealed firearms or other deadly weapons, or a combination thereof, to persons who: (a) Are eighteen (18) years of age but younger than twenty-one (21) years of age; and (b) Notwithstanding KRS 237.110(4)(c), otherwise meet the criteria set forth in KRS 237.110(4) and the requirements of KRS 237.110(3).\nSection 1 (new section of KRS Chapter 237): (4) A provisional license issued pursuant to this section shall: (a) Be valid throughout the Commonwealth and, except as provided in other specific sections of the Kentucky Revised Statutes or federal law, permit the holder of the provisional license to carry firearms, ammunition, other deadly weapons, or a combination thereof, at any location in the Commonwealth; (b) Unless revoked or suspended as provided by law, be valid until the holder turns twenty-one (21) years of age;\nSection 1 (new section of KRS Chapter 237): (6) (a) Not less than ninety (90) days before the expiration of the provisional license, the Department of Kentucky State Police shall mail to the holder of the provisional license a written notice of the expiration and an application to switch from a provisional license to a standard license.\nSection 1 (new section of KRS Chapter 237): (7) A provisional license which has expired shall be void and shall not be valid for any purpose other than surrender to the sheriff in exchange for a standard license."
}